### Key Stakeholders

**1. Teachers**
Key stakeholders because they provide the experience, knowledge, and direction that students rely on throughout their education
This AI should serve as a tool that makes teachers more effective at their jobs.
The AI tool should help teachers focus more on mentoring students and exploring opportunities
To start the project, teacher can begin the process of accumulating program or even “within program” shared knowledge (“canon”) – shared communal knowledge that is built collaboratively by a community of faculty that represents the “knowledge” parts of that program learning goals – evolves over time 

**2. Students**
Are the ones who pay tuition, which ultimately fund the college
The bot is to help them learn more quickly while getting greater value from their education
The AI should help students work more efficiently, get more insights surrounding their topics, complete assignments faster, and reduce the amount of unnecessary time spent on repetitive academic tasks and research
Students get different “topic bots” that reflect a lot of the shared knowing of the faculty in a given topic. That could be program specific, course sequence specific or even course specific. Ensures that the “knowledge exploration” (conversations) are “by design” from the faculty as starting point.

**4. Administrator**
Are the one who execute and bring the school curriculums designed by the head professors into action
Responsibilities: Refine the curriculum / Create a better learning environment for students to have connection in the professional world
Begin the process of accumulating domain knowledge, per program, in a way that can serve students, and grow over time  
Develop community expertise 
Create a better learning environment and build stronger connections with students and alumni. To accomplish this, the AI should help staff complete their daily responsibilities more efficiently while also providing quick access to information. For example, it could function as an HR resource and an always-available assistant that can answer questions that might otherwise take hours to research or require waiting for an HR representative or manager. This would allow staff to spend less time searching for information and more time focusing on their responsibilities and the college community.

